<title>GREECE: GREEK DEP TO UP GASOLINE PRICES, CUT HEATING OIL PRICES THU.</title>
<headline>GREEK DEP TO UP GASOLINE PRICES, CUT HEATING OIL PRICES THU.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece's state Public Petroleum Corporation (DEP) will raise gasoline prices 1.40 drachmas and reduce heating oil prices 0.40 drachmas per litre on January 30, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>The new prices reflect higher international gasoline prices, up $ 0.2/MT, lower motor diesel prices, down $ 7.4/MT, and heating diesel prices, down $ 12/MT, and the appreciation of the dollar against the drachma by 6.40 drachmas per $.</p>
<p>--Margarita Sotiropoulou, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
